        <fig id="article-698.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Isolated Posterior Myocardial Infarction, Graft Occlusion. This 12-lead&#x000a0;electrocardiographic tracing demonstrates ST depression and tall R waves (R/S ratio &#x02265;1 or R-wave amplitude &#x02265;0.7 mV) in leads V1 to V3, consistent with isolated posterior myocardial infarction. Catheterization confirmed 100% occlusion of the saphenous vein graft to the posterior descending artery with&#x000a0;Thrombolysis in Myocardial Infarction (TIMI) 0 flow. Contributed by Alexander Bracey, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Screen__Shot__2019-01-18__at__8.46.44__PM" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-698.s16">
        <fig id="article-698.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Isolated Posterior Myocardial Infarction, Native Vessel Occlusion. This 12-lead electrocardiographic tracing shows horizontal ST depression and tall R waves (R/S ratio &#x02265;1 or R-wave amplitude &#x02265;0.7 mV) in leads V1 to V3, consistent with isolated posterior myocardial infarction. Coronary angiography demonstrated 100% occlusion of the proximal left circumflex artery with Thrombolysis in Myocardial Infarction (TIMI) 0 flow. Contributed by Alexander Bracey, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Isolated__Posterior__MI__xOMIxx__100x__pLCxx__TIMI__0" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
